### Please describe the problem in your own words.

With the most recent version of git-annex (10.20261006) built on macOS 15 / Intel, from a Homebrew Formula (Homebrew no longer builds bottles for macOS Intel, so built locally from the Homebrew Formula) it appears that "addurl" and "importfeed" both crash with "error: git-annex died of signal 4" around the point that the download would be starting.  Other general git-annex features (eg, sync, copy, etc) seem to work okay -- whatever is happening seems to be linked to URL downloads specifically.

The same git-annex version (10.20261006) does work with the HomeBrew bottle build on macOS ARM, for "addurl" / "importfeed", including with the same URLs.

So my assumption is the issue is either macOS Intel specific or my local build specific (which was just "brew upgrade git-annex" that triggers the build).

This was working, on macOS Intel, with a Homebrew locally built version, on the git-annex release from last month (10.20060901), up until the build of 10.20261006 (I didn't build 10.20261005 as that was superceded before I even saw it).

While looking for similar bugs, I found [this 3 year old bug for addurl batch](https://git-annex.branchable.com/projects/datalad/bugs-done/OSX__58___addurl_--batch_--json_spits_out_shortened_output_string__dies_off_with_4/), which seems a similar outcome, but I can't quite figure out what the fix was (seemingly something related to libmagic), and whether a similar local build step is required again.

Is there a known recent macOS Intel build environment change that might be required now to avoid this kind of crash?

Is there some way I can see the build environment used to build the macOS Intel "standalone" packages to see if I can figure out what might be different?

(All installed Homebrew packages are up to date on the system that did the build, and is running Homebrew when having problems.)

### What steps will reproduce the problem?

Build git-annex 10.20261006 on macOS Intel (15) from the Homebrew Formula.

Try to "addurl" a URL in an existing git annex.

Eg:

[[!format sh """
git annex addurl --debug --debug 'https://updates.cdn-apple.com/2023FallFCS/fullrestores/042-55833/C0830847-A2F8-458F-B680-967991820931/UniversalMac_13.6_22G120_Restore.ipsw'
"""]]

or "importfeed", eg:

[[!format sh """
importfeed gathering known urls ok
importfeed https://risky.biz/feeds/risky-business error: git-annex died of signal 4
"""]]

### What version of git-annex are you using? On what operating system?

git-annex 10.20061006, on macOS 15.7.9 (Sequoia) on Intel (i7).

